an unnoted write to a module-level table is refused: true
the same write after note_mutation () is accounted for: true
a second, unnoted writer beside a noted one is refused: true
a note in an unrelated function does not account for the write: true
a shadowing local note_mutation is not the real one: true
Row.note_mutation () is the real one from another module: true
Row.note_mutation () through a locally bound Row is not the real one: true
Row.note_mutation () under a module Row the file binds is not the real one: true
outside the serial's own module, a top-level note_mutation is not the real one: true
a container function through a locally bound Hash_set is not classified: true
an assignment through a shadowing ( := ) is not classified: true
state in an included structure is refused: true
an unlisted constructor hidden under a local let is refused: true
two same-named fingerprinted refs are judged apart: true
a bare note_mutation () that resolves to nothing in this file is not the real one: true
find_or_add with the note in its ~default closure is accounted for: true
find_or_add with no note is refused: true
a write inside an anonymous closure of a noting function is accounted for: true
a write inside a nested let-bound function is judged by that function: true
a write under let%ext is judged like any other: true
:= on an unnoted path is refused: true
incr, Int.incr and Stdlib.incr are writes: true
reading a ref is not a write: true
a ref given to a helper is a use the scan does not classify: true
an array element assignment is Array.set, a write: true
a function-local table is not module-level state: true
a parameter spelled like the table is not the table: true
comments and string literals are not code: true
a container function outside the lists is refused: true
the table escaping to a caller is refused: true
a write at module initialization is refused: true
state hidden under a local let of a module-level value is refused: true
hidden state on an exempt binding is admitted: true
state inside a nested module is refused: true
an allocation by a constructor outside the closed list is refused: true
a mutable allocation bound by a pattern is refused: true
a table the interface exports is refused: true
a table exported through an included signature is refused: true
an interface include of a module type the scan cannot read is refused: true
state an initializer creates in a function it invokes on the spot is refused: true
an interface exporting only functions is fine: true
an exempt binding's unnoted writes are admitted: true
an exemption no write needs is stale: true
a fingerprinted ref mutated_since compares physically needs no note: true
a fingerprinted ref that mutated_since does not read is refused: true
a fingerprinted ref that mutated_since reads but does not compare is refused: true
a fingerprinted ref compared through a shadowing phys_equal is refused: true
only a ref can be fingerprinted: true
a boundary function's writes are admitted: true
a boundary whose function needs none is stale: true
a boundary only excuses its own function: true
a one-word reason is malformed: true
an unknown attribute name is malformed: true
fingerprinted takes no payload: true
an attribute on something it does not classify is refused: true
two classifications on one binding are refused: true
a source that does not parse is the input's fault, not the scanner's: true
